  "question_stem": "A particle moves in a straight line starting from a point $O$. The velocity $v \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ of the particle $t \\text{ s}$ after leaving $O$ is given by $$v = t^3 - \\frac{9}{2}t^2 + 1 \\text{ for } 0 \\le t \\le 4.$$ You may assume that the velocity of the particle is positive for $t < \\frac{1}{2}$, is zero at $t = \\frac{1}{2}$ and is negative for $t > \\frac{1}{2}$.",
